WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:09.000
Wie haben Sie Ihre ersten Jahre im Kibbuz Nahal Oz erlebt? Was hat Sie damals dazu bewegt, dort zu leben?

00:11.800 --> 00:15.633
I came here when I was in my 20s,

00:15.933 --> 00:18.066
I came to study.

00:18.066 --> 00:19.400
There is a very good college,

00:19.400 --> 00:21.800
it's the best in Israel,

00:21.800 --> 00:23.333
about a 10-minute drive from here.

00:23.333 --> 00:24.666
So many people

00:24.700 --> 00:27.400
come to this area in order to become students.

00:27.966 --> 00:29.833
So the reasons

00:30.133 --> 00:33.866
I chose Nahal Oz were because

00:33.866 --> 00:36.900
the rent was fair, they had plenty of young people here,

00:36.900 --> 00:38.666
and they said I could bring my dog,

00:39.166 --> 00:43.666
those were the elements taken into consideration.

00:44.433 --> 00:46.133
My political views...

00:46.133 --> 00:48.666
It had nothing to do with my political views,

00:48.866 --> 00:51.200
I always was,

00:51.300 --> 00:54.100
I was in my entire life left-leaning.

00:54.100 --> 00:56.166
always voted

00:56.300 --> 01:00.200
center-left, and apparently it was a fit,

01:00.200 --> 01:02.333
because the people on the kibbutz,

01:02.333 --> 01:04.233
on this kibbutz,

01:04.300 --> 01:07.533
the numbers are quite astonishing,

01:07.533 --> 01:12.466
92% of the people here used to vote center-left.

01:13.066 --> 01:15.266
We still haven’t had a new election,

01:15.266 --> 01:18.066
so I don’t know what will happen after October 7th,

01:18.633 --> 01:22.300
but this is the left stronghold

01:22.300 --> 01:25.500
of Israel, the Gaza envelope.

01:25.733 --> 01:28.433
People here really believed in

01:29.366 --> 01:31.666
working with the palestinians.

01:32.200 --> 01:33.866
There was...

01:37.266 --> 01:38.300
I'm just...

01:38.366 --> 01:40.600
It will probably come up in the other questions.

01:42.600 --> 01:44.800
So when I arrived here,

01:44.800 --> 01:47.466
I arrived in 2002

01:48.000 --> 01:52.066
and the rockets on Nahal Oz began a year before that.

01:52.500 --> 01:57.000
But still it was very simple rockets,

01:57.000 --> 01:58.400
it wasn't what we have today.

01:58.400 --> 02:01.800
It was like a light-years difference.

02:02.300 --> 02:06.066
Damage from a rocket hit

02:06.066 --> 02:08.966
would be something the size

02:08.966 --> 02:11.966
the size of a regular ashtray.

02:11.966 --> 02:13.700
Something like this and this.

02:14.066 --> 02:16.000
And I still didn’t have children,

02:16.000 --> 02:19.400
which is a huge game changer,

02:21.266 --> 02:23.666
so I came here and

02:24.366 --> 02:27.000
I remember that we were sitting outside.

02:28.500 --> 02:30.633
All the friends, and

02:30.933 --> 02:33.100
in the evening and there was an alarm or something,

02:33.100 --> 02:35.866
we wouldn’t even get up.

02:35.866 --> 02:37.400
Back then.

02:38.533 --> 02:43.166
But then things started escalating seriously after that.
